# The same script with download_media/read_file arguments logged (temporary copy /tmp/nts515/eval-args.mjs), da-download x4 per build:
old rep0 success=false download_media({"url":"https://example.com/logo.png","filename":"logo","folder":"downloads"})
old rep1 success=true download_media({"url":"https://example.com/logo.png","filename":"logo","folder":"downloads"}) | download_media({"filename":"logo.png","folder":"downloads","url":"https://example.com/logo.png"})
old rep2 success=true download_media({"url":"https://example.com/logo.png","filename":"logo"}) | download_media({"filename":"logo.png","folder":"downloads","url":"https://example.com/logo.png"})
old rep3 success=false download_media({"url":"https://example.com/logo.png","filename":"logo","folder":"downloads"})
new rep0 success=false download_media({"url":"https://example.com/logo.png","filename":"logo","folder":"downloads"})
new rep1 success=false download_media({"url":"https://example.com/logo.png","filename":"logo","folder":"downloads"})
new rep2 success=false download_media({"url":"https://example.com/logo.png","filename":"logo","folder":"downloads"})
new rep3 success=false download_media({"url":"https://example.com/logo.png","filename":"logo","folder":"downloads"})
# download_media's schema: 'filename': 'The desired base name ... The tool will automatically add the correct file extension.' The evaluation's stub wrote <folder>/<filename> as given, so a schema-following call (filename 'logo') left downloads/logo and the state check (downloads/logo.png) failed; old runs passed only when the model retried with 'logo.png'.
# Fix (evidence/evaluate-tool-search.mjs, marked "API/E2E fix"): the stub adds the URL extension when filename has none, as the real tool does.

